# === AI / Tooling ===
# `.claude/skills/` IS committed — the roadkeep skill is a vendored copy that
# `roadkeep install --check` keeps in step with the checkout it came from.
# Everything else under .claude/ is local machine state: locks, scheduled-task
# bookkeeping. Note the `*` — git does not descend into an ignored directory, so
# `/.claude/` without it would make the negations below unreachable.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/skills/
# settings.json IS committed: it declares the roadkeep marketplace and enables the
# plugin, so a clone gets the hook, the tools and the skill with no local setup.
!/.claude/settings.json
# hooks/ IS committed: the plugin never installs on Claude Code on the web (no
# `/plugin`), so the committed roadkeep-launch.py is how a cloud session gets the
# guard the plugin would give a local machine.
!/.claude/hooks/
# `roadkeep report` output — a local capture, never a source.
.roadkeep/

# === Test-guest credentials ===
# `dockerdesk-vm.env` in this directory holds the VM encryption password and the guest login that
# `scripts/vm.ps1` drives the Windows test guest with. It lives here for convenience and this line
# is the only thing keeping it out of a commit, so two limits are worth stating: `git add -f`
# stages it anyway, and `git clean -xdf` deletes it without asking. Keep the credential in it one
# that can be rotated cheaply, and never remove this line.
*.env

# === .NET ===
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
*.user
.vs/

# === Build output ===
/dist/

# === Window captures ===
# Both capture paths write here (DD22). The renders are safe by construction, but a screen copy is
# not: this window's backdrop is translucent, so a correctly-cropped, overlap-free copy still carries
# a blurred image of whatever was behind it - measured, with another application's content legible
# through the frame. A capture is a working artefact, never a source, and it does not get staged.
/docs/_preview/
